  "goodToKnow": "Die Kündigungsfrist is the notice period for ending a contract. By law (§622 BGB), employees can give four weeks' notice to the 15th or the end of a month, while employers' notice periods grow with length of service. Tenants generally give three months' notice. Since 2022, many consumer contracts like gym or phone plans can be cancelled monthly after the initial term. Die Frist means deadline. Plural: die Kündigungsfristen."
